# Build
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
# `go build ./cmd/<name>` writes its binary into the working directory rather than into /bin, so
# each one is named here. Without this a stray build lands in a commit, which is how a 30 MB
# `restore-drill` very nearly did - and how a 10 MB `hubctl` did, three times, before its line
# stood here (#640).
/hubtask
/hubtask-migrate
/migrate
/restore-drill
/hubctl
/server

# Dependencies
/vendor/
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# JavaScript build output (ADR-0027). The two deliberate exceptions are un-ignored where they
# stand: presentation/webui/dist/index.html, so that go:embed resolves without a frontend build
# (ADR-0028), and core/domain/model/shared/LabelTokens.go, which is generated into the core and
# is not under any of these paths at all (ADR-0029).
apps/*/dist/
# What `make e2e RECORD=1` writes: the walks' answers, read by `make gate-walks`.
apps/webapp/.walk-record/
packages/*/dist/
sdk/typescript/dist/
.svelte-kit/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
!deploy/docker/.env.example

# Tools
/.tools/
# What `make dev` makes and `make dev-down` removes: binaries, logs, media, generated secrets.
/.dev/
# The coverage profiles gate-unit writes; a wider pattern also matched Coverage.go on macOS.
coverage.out
coverage.*.out
coverage.html
/tmp/
# scripts/gate-selftest.sh writes its violating packages here and removes them again; the entry
# is the safety net for a hard abort.
**/gate_selftest/

# Editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# The embedded UI bundle. Everything the frontend build writes here is generated - except
# index.html, which is committed as a placeholder so that //go:embed resolves and `go build ./...`
# succeeds without Node.js (ADR-0028).
/presentation/webui/dist/*
!/presentation/webui/dist/index.html

# Local Claude Code tooling (launch configurations, settings, worktrees); not project content.
# Three exceptions: settings.json carries the hook that holds a Claude Code session to the draft
# rule of AGENTS.md (ADR-0079); skills/ holds one link per skill of .agents/skills/, where that
# tool looks for them, and agents/ the reviewer's wrapper (ADR-0106).
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/agents/

# Python bytecode from running the SDK example or its test
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The CSAF feed the website build writes from security/advisories/ (make csaf); never committed.
apps/website/static/.well-known/csaf/
